ore than $2.7 million in outside support, while Republican Riley Owen has raised about $150,000. No expert raters cover the race, but the district's structural lean combined with a favorable national environment points clearly toward Democrats.\n\nThe only public poll, a September survey of likely voters, put McAdams ahead 63 to 21, and prediction markets price his chances near 96 to 97 percent. The campaign has drawn sustained debate attention on prices, artificial intelligence, and data centers, but Owen has yet to show the resources or polling movement needed to close a gap this wide. Minor-party candidates are on the ballot but appear unlikely to change the outcome.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9908, "margin": 20.9}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.99, "margin": 20.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.9893, "margin": 21.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.9909, "margin": 21.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.9895, "margin": 21.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.9899, "margin": 21.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.9906, "margin": 21.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.9886, "margin": 20.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.9895, "margin": 20.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.9907, "margin": 21.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.99, "margin": 21.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.9979, "margin": 28.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.9958, "margin": 26.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.997, "margin": 27.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.9991, "margin": 28.0}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.9988, "margin": 27.0}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.9979, "margin": 27.0}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.9971, "margin": 27.0}, {"date": "2026-10-10", "p_dem": 0.9972, "margin": 26.0}, {"date": "2026-10-11", "p_dem": 0.9981, "margin": 25.0}, {"date": "2026-10-12", "p_dem": 0.9972, "margin": 26.0}, {"date": "2026-10-13", "p_dem": 0.997, "margin": 26.0}, {"date": "2026-10-14", "p_dem": 0.997, "margin": 26.0}, {"d